   "angle": 0,
   "seed": 100027,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 700189,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "groupIds": [],
   "boundElements": null,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "Two of those rows change the design fundamentally. It is WRITE-HEAVY - nearly unique among search systems - because every\nreceived email, every send and every metadata change is an index write: 40 billion index writes/day against maybe a few\nhundred million queries. So the engine must be optimized for INGEST, not for query throughput.",
   "originalText": "Two of those rows change the design fundamentally. It is WRITE-HEAVY - nearly unique among search systems - because every\nreceived email, every send and every metadata change is an index write: 40 billion index writes/day against maybe a few\nhundred million queries. So the engine must be optimized for INGEST, not for query throughput.",
   "fontSize": 13,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
  {
   "id": "an2",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 30,
   "y": 424,
   "width": 1019,
   "height": 48,
   "strokeColor": "#b91c1c",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 1,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "angle": 0,
   "seed": 100028,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 700196,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "groupIds": [],
   "boundElements": null,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "And RESULTS MUST BE EXACT. Web search returning the best 10 of a million matches is a feature; email search failing to surface\na message the user knows exists is a bug, and the kind users notice and remember. So there is no room for the\napproximate-recall techniques that make web-scale search affordable.",
   "originalText": "And RESULTS MUST BE EXACT. Web search returning the best 10 of a million matches is a feature; email search failing to surface\na message the user knows exists is a bug, and the kind users notice and remember. So there is no room for the\napproximate-recall techniques that make web-scale search affordable.",
   "fontSize": 13,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
  {
   "id": "an3",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 30,
   "y": 498,
   "width": 1011,
   "height": 32,
   "strokeColor": "#047857",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 1,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "angle": 0,
   "seed": 100029,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 700203,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "groupIds": [],
   "boundElements": null,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "The one thing that makes it tractable: THE QUERY SCOPE IS ONE MAILBOX. A search never spans users, so the index partitions by\nuser_id and every query is single-partition over a small dataset. That property is doing all the work below.",
   "originalText": "The one thing that makes it tractable: THE QUERY SCOPE IS ONE MAILBOX. A search never spans users, so the index partitions by\nuser_id and every query is single-partition over a small dataset. That property is doing all the work below.",
   "fontSize": 13,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
  {
