  },
  {
   "id": "idx_t",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 38,
   "y": 632,
   "width": 764,
   "height": 90,
   "strokeColor": "#ffffff",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 1,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "angle": 0,
   "seed": 100033,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 700231,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "groupIds": [],
   "boundElements": null,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "INDEXED - immutable, safe to index once and never rewrite\n    subject, body (plain text extracted from HTML), from, to, cc,\n    attachment filenames, attachment text content, date\n\nNOT INDEXED - mutable, lives only in the metadata store\n    is_read, folder_id, labels, is_starred",
   "originalText": "INDEXED - immutable, safe to index once and never rewrite\n    subject, body (plain text extracted from HTML), from, to, cc,\n    attachment filenames, attachment text content, date\n\nNOT INDEXED - mutable, lives only in the metadata store\n    is_read, folder_id, labels, is_starred",
   "fontSize": 12,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "middle",
   "containerId": "idx",
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
  {
   "id": "bn",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 860,
   "y": 612,
   "width": 584,
   "height": 60,
   "strokeColor": "#b91c1c",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 1,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "angle": 0,
   "seed": 100034,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 700238,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "groupIds": [],
   "boundElements": null,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "Lucene documents are IMMUTABLE, so marking an email read means writing a\ntombstone and indexing a whole new document - reindexing the entire 50 KB body\nto flip a boolean. A brutal amplification for the single most common metadata\nchange in the product, and the detail that matters most.",
   "originalText": "Lucene documents are IMMUTABLE, so marking an email read means writing a\ntombstone and indexing a whole new document - reindexing the entire 50 KB body\nto flip a boolean. A brutal amplification for the single most common metadata\nchange in the product, and the detail that matters most.",
   "fontSize": 12,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
  {
   "id": "bn2",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 860,
   "y": 694,
   "width": 584,
   "height": 60,
   "strokeColor": "#64748b",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 1,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "angle": 0,
   "seed": 100035,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 700245,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "groupIds": [],
   "boundElements": null,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "So: index only the immutable content, and keep mutable state in the metadata\nstore. A search becomes two steps - query the index for matching message_ids,\nthen filter and enrich from the metadata store - which converts 'reindex 50 KB\nto flip a bit' into 'update one small row'.",
   "originalText": "So: index only the immutable content, and keep mutable state in the metadata\nstore. A search becomes two steps - query the index for matching message_ids,\nthen filter and enrich from the metadata store - which converts 'reindex 50 KB\nto flip a bit' into 'update one small row'.",
   "fontSize": 12,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
